## 📁 Project Structure

The project follows a **full stack architecture** with separate frontend and backend directories.

```
smartresumebuilder/
│
├── backend/
│   ├── middleware/        # Custom middleware (auth, error handling)
│   ├── models/            # Mongoose schemas (User, Resume, Job)
│   ├── routes/            # API route definitions
│   ├── node_modules/      # Backend dependencies
│   ├── .env               # Environment variables
│   ├── server.js          # Entry point of backend server
│   ├── package.json       # Backend dependencies & scripts
│
├── frontend/
│   ├── public/            # Static assets
│   ├── src/               # React source code
│   │   ├── components/    # Reusable UI components
│   │   ├── pages/         # Application pages (Login, Dashboard, etc.)
│   │   ├── context/       # Global state management (Context API)
│   │   ├── hooks/         # Custom React hooks
│   │   ├── services/      # API calls and utilities
│   ├── node_modules/      # Frontend dependencies
│   ├── index.html         # Main HTML file
│   ├── package.json       # Frontend dependencies & scripts
│   ├── vite.config.js     # Vite configuration
│   ├── tailwind.config.js # Tailwind CSS configuration
│   ├── postcss.config.js  # PostCSS configuration
│   ├── eslint.config.js   # Linting configuration
│   ├── .gitignore         # Ignored files
│   ├── README.md          # Frontend documentation
│
├── package-lock.json      # Root dependency lock file (if any)
│
└── README.md              # Main project documentation
```

---

## 🧩 Architecture Overview

* **Frontend**: Built using React + Tailwind CSS for a responsive and modern UI
* **Backend**: Node.js + Express.js for handling APIs and business logic
* **Database**: MongoDB for storing users, resumes, and job data

---

## 🔄 Data Flow

1. User interacts with the frontend (React UI)
2. Frontend sends API requests to backend (Express)
3. Backend processes logic and interacts with MongoDB
4. Response is sent back and displayed in UI

